From 50025339171c4c024bf5fd6f4934d975917103aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zambia Treasury Insight <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:22:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Tier 1 #2: .env.example documents all env vars

Lists every ZTI_* variable the app reads (DB path, auth, auto-ingest, refresh
hours) plus the RENDER signal Render sets itself. Adds .env to .gitignore so
local devs can copy .env.example to .env without leaking secrets.

render.yaml already sets the structural env vars; this file is the human-readable
documentation that goes alongside it.
---
 .env.example | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 .gitignore   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .env.example

diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..23292b0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Zambia Treasury Insight — environment variables
+# Copy this file to `.env` for local development (then never commit `.env`).
+# On Render, set these in the dashboard under Environment; never put real secrets
+# in render.yaml (use `sync: false` and type them in the UI).
+
+# --- Database ---
+# SQLite path. Default: data/zti.sqlite (relative to repo root). For tests use /tmp.
+# Render uses an ephemeral disk: the DB is rebuilt from seed files + live ingest on each boot.
+ZTI_DB=data/zti.sqlite
+
+# --- Authentication (optional but recommended on a public host) ---
+# If ZTI_PASSWORD is set, every endpoint except /api/health requires HTTP Basic Auth.
+# If you deploy on Render without this, data controls (upload/refresh/demo) are
+# locked server-side to prevent anonymous users from corrupting the data.
+ZTI_USER=treasury
+# ZTI_PASSWORD=  # set on Render; never commit a real value to git
+
+# --- Background refresh ---
+# ZTI_AUTO_INGEST=1 -> on boot, ingest live data if DB empty, then refresh every ZTI_REFRESH_HOURS.
+# Defaults to "on" when RENDER=true is present in the environment.
+ZTI_AUTO_INGEST=1
+ZTI_REFRESH_HOURS=12
+
+# --- Render-only signal (do not set locally) ---
+# Render sets RENDER=true automatically. The app uses it to detect a public host
+# and to default ZTI_AUTO_INGEST on.
+# RENDER=true
diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index a8b9eee..5f77bec 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+.env
 __pycache__/
 *.pyc
 .pytest_cache/
